@using MLQT.Shared
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using static Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web.RenderMode

@*
    Prerendering is off, and that is not a preference. A webview host renders interactively from the
    first frame; Blazor Server by default renders the component tree statically on the server first.
    MLQT's components issue JS interop during their initial render, which is legal in a webview and
    throws during a static render - the first request to this host was a 500 for exactly that reason.
    Prerendering here would make journeys fail on a difference the product does not have.
*@
@{ var interactive = new InteractiveServerRenderMode(prerender: false); }

@*
    The test host's page. Deliberately *generated* from HostAssetManifest rather than hand-written,
    which makes drift impossible for this host by construction. The Photino host's page is
    hand-written - it is a static file the webview loads, with no Razor underneath it - and is held
    to the same manifest by HostAssetManifestTests instead.
*@

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>MLQT (test host)</title>
    <base href="/" />

    @foreach (var stylesheet in HostAssetManifest.Stylesheets)
    {
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="@stylesheet" />
    }
    <link rel="icon" href="data:," />

    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="interactive" />
</head>
<body>
    <Routes @rendermode="interactive" />

    @* The bootstrap script is the one line that differs between hosts. *@
    <script src="@HostAssetManifest.ServerBootstrapScript"></script>

    @foreach (var script in HostAssetManifest.Scripts)
    {
        <script src="@script"></script>
    }

    @*
        The inline helper every host page carries. Probe 1 of the /selftest route in 7a-7 exists
        because losing it breaks every measurement the UI makes of its own window.
    *@
    <script>
        window.getDimensions = function () {
            return { width: window.innerWidth, height: window.innerHeight };
        };
    </script>
</body>
</html>
